From 139824f85fccf7873328db06ab4ccc9d4b500bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: morgonf <morgonf@altlinux.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:51:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Night mode: a burst of 12 frames aligned and merged

The moon button in the header switches it on (photo mode only). The
shutter then takes 12 frames from the binned viewfinder stream with the
exposure held, shows a progress bar and asks to hold the phone still.
NightMerge aligns them to the sharpest frame (global shift on a luma
pyramid), averages them leaving out what moved, and lifts the shadows.
Frames may last up to 1/4 s in night mode (FrameDurationLimits).
On a synthetic burst with known shifts all shifts were found and the
noise fell 3.44x (sqrt(12) = 3.46).
