From a0bcfa3b8807350d36659cbee8cadf773c0a6118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: morgonf <morgonf@altlinux.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:35:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Flash: off, automatic and on, with autofocus assist

A button in the header cycles the flash of the rear cameras (the flash_*
LED class interface, writable through an ALT Mobile udev rule). Auto
fires at 4x analogue gain or more. The shutter first waits for short
frames with the torch on and runs a focus search (autofocus assist),
then strobes both LEDs at 0.75 A each, lets AE follow the flash light
and takes the frame once the exposure has settled, at most 1 s into the
1.28 s strobe. The night mode hint and progress bar show meanwhile.
